{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "1CO",
  "chapter": 9,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Am I not an apostle? am I not free? have I not seen Jesus Christ our Lord? are ye not my work in the Lord?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I am not an apostle to others, yet doubtless I am to you: for ye are the seal of my apostleship in the Lord.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My answer to them that examine me is this,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Have we not power to eat and to drink?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Have we not power to lead about a sister, a wife, as well as other apostles, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the brethren of the Lord, and Cephas?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Or I only and Barnabas, have we not power to forbear working?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who goeth a warfare at any time at his own charges? who planteth a vineyard, and eateth not of its fruit? or who feedeth a flock, and eateth not of the milk of the flock?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do I say these things as a man? or saith not the law the same also?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For it is written in the law of Moses, Thou shalt not muzzle the mouth of the ox that treadeth out the corn. Doth God take care for oxen?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Or saith he ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "this",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " altogether for our sakes? for our sakes, no doubt, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "this",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " is written: that he that ploweth should plow in hope; and that he that thresheth in hope should be partaker of his hope.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If we have sown to you spiritual things, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a great thing if we shall reap your carnal things?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If others are partakers of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "this",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " power over you, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not we rather? Nevertheless we have not used this power; but suffer all things, lest we should hinder the gospel of Christ.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do ye not know that they who minister about holy things live ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "from the things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the temple, and they who wait at the altar are partakers with the altar?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Even so hath the Lord ordained that they who preach the gospel should live by the gospel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But I have used none of these things: neither have I written these things, that it should be so done to me: for ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " better for me to die, than that any man should make my glorying void.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For though I preach the gospel, I have nothing to boast of: for necessity is laid upon me; and woe is to me, if I preach not the gospel!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For if I do this thing willingly, I have a reward: but if against my will, a dispensation ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the gospel",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " is committed to me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What is my reward then? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Verily",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that, when I preach the gospel, I may make the gospel of Christ without charge, that I may not abuse my power in the gospel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For though I am free from all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", yet I have made myself servant to all, that I might gain the more.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And to the Jews I became as a Jew, that I might gain the Jews; to them that are under the law, as under the law, that I might gain them that are under the law;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To them that are without law, as without law, (being not without law to God, but under the law to Christ,) that I might gain them that are without law.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To the weak I became as weak, that I might gain the weak: I have become all things to all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", that I might by all means save some.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And this I do for the gospel's sake, that I may be partaker of it with ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "you",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Know ye not, that they who run in a race, all run, but one receiveth the prize? So run, that ye may obtain.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And every man that striveth for the mastery is temperate in all things. Now they ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "do it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to obtain a corruptible crown; but we an incorruptible.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I therefore so run, not as uncertainly; so I fight, not as one that beateth the air:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.9.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.9.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But I keep under my body, and bring ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " into subjection: lest by any means when I have preached to others, I myself should be a cast-away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
